    <statement><p>Find the equation of the hyperbola with the given properties</p>
<p>Vertices <m>(0,-4)</m>, <m>(0,3)</m> and foci  <m>(0, -11)</m>, <m>(0,10)</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>=1</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(\frac{y+0.5}{3.5}\right)^{2}-\frac{x^{2}}{98}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\left(0,\frac{-4 + 3}{2}\right) = \left(0,-0.5\right)</m>. 

 Thus, the equation has the form 
<m>{\left(\frac{y+ 0.5}{b}\right)}^{2}-{\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)}^{2}=1</m>. 


Since <m>b = 3.5</m> and <m>c = 10.5</m>, we quickly find that 
<m>a^2 = 98</m>, giving us the equation
<me>{\left(\frac{y+ 0.5}{3.5}\right)}^{2}-{\frac{x^2}{98}}=1.</me>


</solution>
